-- title:
--   Dedekind: regular x dt gives Tr(xb) polynomial in t
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and $F$ a field extension of $K$ which is a curve over $K$ in the sense of the predicate [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15): every nonzero $f\in F$ has a degree-zero divisor whose value at each place is $\operatorname{ord}_v f$, each place has residue field finite-dimensional over $K$, and $\Omega[F\!\;\!/K]$ is free of rank one over $F$; here a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, and $\operatorname{ord}_v$ is minus the logarithm of its associated adic valuation. Let $t\in F$ be transcendental over $K$, with $F$ finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(t)$ generated by $t$. Let $x\in F$ be such that for every place $w$ with $\operatorname{ord}_w t\ge 0$ there is an element $g$ of the valuation subring of $w$ with $x\cdot D_{K/F}(t)=g\cdot D_{K/F}(\pi_w)$ in $\Omega[F\!\;\!/K]$, where $\pi_w$ is the uniformiser of $w$ chosen by `AlgebraicCurve.dCoord`. Let $b\in F$ be integral over the $K$-subalgebra $K[t]$ generated by $t$. Then there is a polynomial $P$ over $K$ such that the trace of $xb$ from $F$ to $K(t)$, viewed in $F$, equals $P(t)$.
--
--   This is one half of Dedekind's theorem relating the module of differentials to the inverse different, in the geometric form: regularity of $x\,dt$ at all places where $t$ is finite places $x$ in the complementary module of the integral closure of $K[t]$ in $F$, so that all traces $\operatorname{Tr}_{F/K(t)}(xb)$ with $b$ integral over $K[t]$ are polynomials in $t$. It is used in the treatment of regular differentials on modular curves, where $t$ is the $j$-function and the traces are recognised as $q$-expansion coefficients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_trace_mul_eq_aeval_of_forall_exists_smul_D_eq_smul_dCoord.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_RegularDifferentials
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.exists_trace_mul_eq_aeval_of_forall_exists_smul_D_eq_smul_dCoord
    {K F : Type*} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F] [IsAlgClosed K] [AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver K F]
    (t : F) (ht : Transcendental K t)
    [FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) F]
    (x : F)
    (hx : ∀ w : AlgebraicCurve.Place K F, 0 ≤ w.ord t →
      ∃ g ∈ w.toValuationSubring, x • KaehlerDifferential.D K F t = g • w.dCoord)
    (b : F) (hb : IsIntegral (Algebra.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) b) :
    ∃ P : Polynomial K,
      ((Algebra.trace (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) F (x * b) :
          IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) : F) = Polynomial.aeval t P := by sorry
